WEBVTT

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.900
<i>I don't get it.</i>

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.030
Okay, let's play baseball together.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.230
If you return to the Dolphins,

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:19.740
I'll try to figure out the appeal of 
baseball by playing some more.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:20.870
What?!

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:22.620
Where did that come from?!

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.560
I'm telling you—the person with 
<i>actual</i> talent—not to quit!

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.620
What does that have to do with me?!

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:34.720
Talent or no talent aside, 
playing baseball gets you pumped.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:37.920
You love baseball.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.250
You've inherited the talent for 
loving the game from your father.

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:49.420
Stop caring about what other people think.

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:53.530
If anyone even thinks about
mocking you, I'll fire them into the sun!

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:58.300
So you'd better be at practice this week.

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:06.000
<i>That guy... I swear...</i>

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:10.000
I don't get him at all!

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:44.930
Huh? Where's it gone?

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.370
I could've sworn it was right...

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:49.030
Found it.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:56.440
The Talent of Loving Baseball

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.110
Huh?

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.210
Daigo!

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:15.630
Daigo, look at you! Getting all into it.

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:18.510
Let go of me!

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:22.000
I'm only doing this to get that console.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.650
You'd better keep your promise this time.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:26.600
Whatever floats your boat!

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:30.570
Oh, we've got to buy you a glove.
A cheap one will be fine.

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:31.640
It's fine.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.200
I've got a glove.

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:36.500
But how?

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.830
Izumi told me you got rid of it.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.170
Well, you see... I didn't actually throw it away.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.840
I see. Well, just do your best
without overextending yourself.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.170
Just be yourself, yeah?

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:57.860
Play baseball your own way.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.070
Okay, gimme money for the console.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:03.980
That's a separate matter.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:21.340
Morning, Daigo-kun.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:22.700
I knew you'd come.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:26.030
I'm only here because you told me to come.

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:30.180
Wanna get started?

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:32.370
Sure.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:37.790
Hey, why are you using a catcher's mitt?

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:41.180
It's all we had at my house.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:45.600
I see.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:47.970
Your father's a catcher, right?

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.160
Nice ball.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:56.310
Oh, yeah. Is there any particular 
position you want to play?

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:02.720
I played center field in the last game, but 
the ball didn't come my way all that often.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.070
It was quite boring out there.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:08.360
Hey, catching a fly ball in the outfield
can get <i>very</i> exciting.

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:10.530
You stand out, and all eyes are on you!

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:11.880
"Stand out"?

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:12.790
That's it!

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:18.130
If I'm going to do this, I want to 
be in the most visible position.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:23.880
W-Well, the most visible position 
on the field would be the pitcher.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:27.180
Back when my dad was 
still pitching in the majors...

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:33.020
Every single time he threw the ball, 
the capacity crowd cheered.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.830
When he struck someone out, they roared.

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:40.070
I only got to see it on TV, though.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:45.860
So baseball's star is the pitcher.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.630
That sounds like it might not be so boring...

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:51.200
I've decided to become a pitcher!

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:12.260
Hey! How are you going to pitch 
with control like that?!

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:13.600
Idiot!

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:16.090
Who are these losers?

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:20.100
Them? They're the new guys 
who joined last week.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:21.770
Let's go rip on them.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:25.980
Jeez... And he thinks he can be a pitcher?

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:33.740
You're really the son of Satou Toshiya?!

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:36.120
Yup. I'm Satou Hikaru.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:39.950
But seeing the kid of a pro
isn't <i>that </i>rare, is it?

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:42.640
I mean, Daigo-kun here is the son 
of <i>the</i> Shigeno Goro.

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:44.740
Seriously?

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:45.980
Yeah.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:51.030
These guys weren't at the last game 
because they came down with the flu.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:54.510
Apparently, they joined the Dolphins
around a year ago.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:57.850
Oh, okay. So that's why they don't know me.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:02.690
So we've gained two powerful weapons
to stick on our roster at this odd time?

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:03.980
This is good.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:08.320
I'm Urabe. I'm the Dolphins' ace.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:10.280
And this is Andy, our starting catcher.

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:15.370
We'd love to see what kind of skills 
thoroughbreds like you are packing!

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:18.700
How about we have a pick-up game?

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:20.940
A-A-A pick-up game?

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:23.980
Oh, no, we're nothing special, really...

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:24.700
Right?

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:25.630
Sounds great!

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:26.910
Let's do it!

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:29.280
All right, to the plate.

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:30.870
Andy, put on your gear.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:31.740
Gotcha.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:35.660
What the hell are you doing, Hikaru?

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:39.130
He's the team's ace.
We're just going to embarrass ourselves!

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:41.790
You won't know that until you give it a go.

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:42.440
What?

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:45.260
And even if we embarrass ourselves... So what?

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:49.440
You really need to just 
stop caring about that.

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:53.040
There's nothing wrong with 
a little embarrassment.

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:58.580
But it's definitely wrong to let potential 
embarrassment get in the way of curiosity.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:02.800
Hey, let's get going already!

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:04.250
Which one of you is up first?

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:09.000
Okay. I'll bat first.

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:24.190
<i>The son of an ex-player who 
played in the majors, huh?</i>

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:29.570
Watch out!

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:35.950
Oops, sorry about that!

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:37.300
That jerk!

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:41.550
Wow. I didn't expect our ace 
to have such poor control.

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:44.790
Guess I actually could
 take that spot for myself.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:50.000
<i>Is that idiot really serious
about becoming a pitcher?</i>

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.850
<i>I have poor control, huh?</i>

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:52.920
<i>Don't be stupid.</i>

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:57.470
<i>I was aiming for your face!</i>

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:02.170
That's in.

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:03.200
Strike.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:04.810
Yep.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:07.150
<i>Dang, that was fast!</i>

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:11.950
<i>You think you can turn up the summer 
before we graduate and start pitching?</i>

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:14.200
<i>Dream on!</i>

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:19.450
What are they doing?

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.580
<i>You're the son of a pro.</i>

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:23.100
<i>So what?</i>

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:25.080
<i>You think I'm scared of you?</i>

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.970
I'm the king here.

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:41.430
Don't you ever mouth off at me again!

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.730
You caught it, so I guess that means I lose.

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:02.250
Even if you middle it,
you're out if it's right at a fielder.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:05.580
That's what I don't like about baseball.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:07.610
<i>Th-This punk...</i>

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:10.040
<i>He made contact on his first time facing me!</i>

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:10.780
Hey!

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:12.290
What are you kids doing here?

00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:16.680
This is dangerous. That's why we don't 
allow players to play pick-up games.

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:20.500
Urabe! Andy! You two should know this!

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:22.510
Sheesh.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:24.100
Coach.

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:27.310
Why have you let new players
join so late in the season?

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:30.560
What do you mean, "why"?

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:33.320
Because new players are 
welcome to join anytime.

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:38.450
These new players are gonna 
force others to sit out games.

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:43.680
This is the last summer 
for the sixth graders.

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:45.020
How is that fair?

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:51.400
They shouldn't be allowed to join the team.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:06.550
Is this supposed to be a joke? Taking in 
two sixth graders so late in the season...

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:13.190
But we haven't even decided if Satou 
or Shigeno will be regulars or not.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:17.080
Of <i>course</i> they'll become regulars.
Well, I'm not sure about short stuff here.

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:21.640
The speccy one's already 
smashing Urabe's pitches.

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:25.890
He's even talking about pitching himself.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:27.650
What?

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:29.330
A-Are you serious, Satou?

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:33.830
Well, it does look like 
the funnest position.

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:38.670
That's enough, Andy.

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:40.890
Don't get so worked up.

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:43.680
We also joined as fifth graders.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.970
Let's all play ball together and have fun.

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:47.300
Urabe?

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:50.490
We don't have that many 
players right now, anyway.

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:54.060
More hands to make up the 
numbers isn't a bad thing.

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.310
Right, sir?

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:57.400
Y-Yeah...

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:02.950
We're simming one out,
runners on the corners.

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:05.030
Let's go, Urabe!

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:06.360
Okay.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.700
<i>Maybe he's not such a bad guy, after all?</i>

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:18.130
Out!

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:20.740
Nice play, Andy.

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.260
All right, that's it!

00:12:29.260 --> 00:12:31.060
Time for some situational 
batting practice!

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:37.900
What the hell was all that about?

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:40.320
You're gonna let them get away with joining?

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:46.160
You honestly think that four-eyed punk
can steal my spot as ace?

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:47.800
N-No...

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:51.840
You're probably more worried about 
one of them taking your place, huh?

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:52.830
What?!

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:54.280
Just listen.

00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:55.970
We just won't let them.

00:12:57.360 --> 00:13:02.360
We're going to show them that their 
parents' fame means nothing here!

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:04.700
R-Right.

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:05.770
Hey!

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:08.550
Satou. Daigo. Come over here.

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:09.350
Yes, sir!

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:15.480
You're interested in pitching, huh, Satou?

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:16.270
Yes, sir.

00:13:16.530 --> 00:13:20.080
Is there any position you're 
interested in, Daigo?

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:24.150
Oh, uh, as long as I'm on the 
field playing, anywhere's fine.

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:26.670
Daigo-kun, you're free to come out and say it.

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:29.340
Just tell him what position 
you'd most like to play.

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:30.980
Shut up.

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:34.330
I'm done with all that idealistic crap.

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:38.900
Even if I said "pitcher," 
it's not gonna happen.

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:42.020
Wh-Why don't you give it some thought, Daigo?

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:43.830
We're going to test you out.

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:45.800
I'll catch, you throw.

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:46.890
Yes, sir!

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:21.680
<i>Was Hikaru's control always this good?</i>

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:23.460
<i>I see.</i>

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:25.260
<i>He has a scary amount of potential.</i>

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:28.830
<i>However...</i>

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:44.660
<i>That's more like it.</i>

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:47.740
<i>The first one was beginner's luck.</i>

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:50.530
<i>Not surprising, given that his 
form is all over the place.</i>

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:54.450
Getting a strike is hard.

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:56.120
What the hell was that?

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:59.700
Other than speed,
his pitching skills are garbage.

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.500
He won't even be a number two like that.

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:06.680
I'm sorry, Satou, but you can't
 be a pitcher for us just yet.

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:07.470
What?

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:10.800
You've got a good arm, though,
so I'm hoping you'll do well in the outfield.

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:14.550
Don't get me wrong.
You have plenty of potential.

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:17.860
But we've only got a month 
until the tournament,

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:21.440
and there's just no way I can
 put a novice in at pitcher.

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:24.850
I understand.

00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:26.780
For now, the outfield will do.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:31.190
Could you give me one more chance, though?

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:32.320
One more chance?

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:36.200
One more pitching tryout 
before the tournament.

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:40.580
You can decide if I can pitch or not then.

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:43.120
U-Uh... sure.

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:47.740
<i>Wh-Why do I already have 
a bad feeling about this?</i>

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:52.630
What? I thought he threw his glove away.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:53.590
Well, he didn't!

00:15:54.210 --> 00:16:00.590
Not letting you have it means
a part of his heart was still in baseball.

00:16:00.590 --> 00:16:04.880
Yeah, I wonder. I bet he only did it 
because he wanted a new console.

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:08.610
He'll give up again soon enough.

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:10.360
What are you talking about?

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:12.740
He's not going to quit this time.

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:14.010
If you say so.

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:27.090
Daigo!

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:30.720
Jeez...

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:34.280
You wake up Sunday morning and as soon 
as you're up, it's games, games, games.

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:36.560
You were so enthusiastic about baseball!

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:38.310
Wasn't it fun?

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:42.640
It was...

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:47.460
But it looks like I'm not 
going to become a regular.

00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:50.160
There's only one month till the tournament.

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:53.280
Joining this late means you're 
not going to get a position

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:55.780
unless you're really good.

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:01.720
Gotta be at least as good as Satou Hikaru.

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:22.450
What?!

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:25.780
Wow, this is amazing!

00:17:25.780 --> 00:17:27.660
I just knew your place would be boss.

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:29.980
You guys even have a batting cage and a pool.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:31.900
What's wrong with you guys?

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:35.360
Don't make my house a pit stop on your date.

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:37.160
We're not on a date!

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:38.780
Anyway, I'm going home now.

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:40.320
Thanks for walking me over.

00:17:41.550 --> 00:17:42.870
What was that about?

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:47.070
I didn't know where you lived, 
so I asked Sakura-san to show me.

00:17:47.070 --> 00:17:48.410
Practice with me, please.

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:49.130
Huh?!

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:51.020
Why do I have to?

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:52.130
Why not?

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:55.990
I can't practice pitching without a catcher.

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:59.890
You're the only one I can ask. Please!

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:01.940
What does that have to do with anything?

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:04.640
Come on. Just for a little bit.

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:10.400
Give me that mitt, then. You can have this one.

00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:16.650
Huh? This glove's quite hard, isn't it?

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:20.260
Yeah, I threw it away once.

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:20.990
Huh?

00:18:21.470 --> 00:18:23.200
When I was trying to quit baseball.

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:42.660
But I couldn't throw it far,

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:44.750
so it washed up on the shore again.

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:49.420
With my weak arm, I couldn't 
even throw my glove away.

00:18:52.620 --> 00:18:56.440
Well, anyway, it's the glove Pop bought for me.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:58.570
It's been in storage.

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:02.570
I'm envious.

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:06.020
You have such an important glove.

00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:06.700
Huh?

00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:09.680
I'm grateful that I get to use it today!

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:15.480
Yo, hold on a second!

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:16.050
Huh?

00:19:17.020 --> 00:19:19.050
What's with your grip?!

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:21.120
What's wrong with it?

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:24.900
You were holding the ball 
like that the entire time?!

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:25.800
Yes?

00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:27.940
It's totally wrong!

00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:32.520
You put your index and middle 
fingers on the stitching like this,

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:36.960
then your thumb and ring finger 
support it from the bottom.

00:19:39.260 --> 00:19:40.750
Your grip's too tight, as well.

00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:43.490
Relax and try a lighter grip.

00:19:43.490 --> 00:19:46.010
Huh? I never knew.

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:46.830
Sheesh...

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:50.360
Anyway, that grip's been directly 
passed down from Shigeno Goro.

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:52.120
Wow.

00:19:52.530 --> 00:19:56.790
Seriously, though, didn't your father 
teach you any of the basics?

00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:58.080
No...

00:19:58.080 --> 00:20:02.680
When I played catch with Papa,
I was still pretty small.

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:06.300
Well, I hope you're grateful.

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:09.220
Yes, I am. Thanks, Daigo-kun.

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:13.680
I'll throw it gently at first!

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:17.820
<i>Gently or not, with </i>your<i> control...</i>

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:23.030
Hey, looking good!

00:20:23.440 --> 00:20:25.240
<i>A-Are you serious?</i>

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:26.490
<i>This guy!</i>

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:29.740
<i>Just by changing his grip...</i>

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:32.620
<i>he's already fixed his control issue?!</i>

00:20:35.030 --> 00:20:38.170
I see! It really is much 
easier to control it this way!

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:39.320
Hey!

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:42.280
You're already throwing at 
full force, aren't you?!

00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:44.100
Huh? Not at all.

00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:46.510
That was totally casual.

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:47.550
What?

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:49.220
If I throw it at full force...

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:52.310
...it's like this!

00:21:00.470 --> 00:21:02.380
All right, nice!

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:05.070
Even at full force, I can control the ball.

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:09.340
All right. Now I've gotta work 
on fine tuning my aim...

00:21:13.530 --> 00:21:14.660
Daigo-kun?

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:16.080
What is this thing?

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:20.050
It's a board my dad built for 
me to practice my pitching.

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:22.920
Anyway, best of luck.

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:24.880
I've got homework to do.

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:27.390
W-Wait! Daigo-kun!

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:28.620
Don't go!

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:30.720
Throwing the ball at a 
wall by myself is boring!

00:21:30.920 --> 00:21:32.830
Be my catcher, come on!

00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:34.810
I'll die!

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:38.660
Do you even know how fast the 
balls you're pitching are going?

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:41.880
Something like 110—no, 120 kmph!

00:21:41.880 --> 00:21:43.530
That's a lethal weapon! Totally lethal!

00:21:43.880 --> 00:21:46.340
You're exaggerating. It's rubber—

00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:49.550
<i>Solid</i> rubber! If it hadn't
 bounced off my mitt,

00:21:49.550 --> 00:21:51.480
I would've been seriously hurt!

00:21:51.480 --> 00:21:53.830
Asking me to catch without 
a mask and chest protector?

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:55.590
What kind of punishment is that?!

00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:59.240
Then, let's go ask the manager 
if we can borrow some.

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:04.430
Look here. Why do I have to go 
that far just to catch for you?

00:22:04.430 --> 00:22:06.320
I'm not even a catcher.

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:11.430
Then, you should become a catcher.

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:12.450
Huh?

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:15.710
That's it! That's a great idea, Daigo-kun.

00:22:15.710 --> 00:22:17.520
You should make becoming 
a catcher your goal!

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:19.930
You learn how to catch my pitches,

00:22:19.930 --> 00:22:23.270
and then, we can challenge 
the Urabe and Andy battery!

00:22:23.800 --> 00:22:25.520
M-Me?

00:22:26.120 --> 00:22:27.920
A catcher?!

00:24:00.630 --> 00:24:01.960
I never even considered it.

00:24:02.620 --> 00:24:04.960
Me, a catcher? With my weak arm?

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:06.700
No, no, no, it's impossible!

00:24:07.580 --> 00:24:10.590
But if I <i>was</i> able to catch Hikaru's pitches...

00:24:11.830 --> 00:24:12.930
All right!

00:24:12.930 --> 00:24:15.090
I'm going to give this a serious try!

00:24:15.310 --> 00:24:18.910
Wait, Mom, what's with your getup?!

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:25.020
Commence Special Training!

00:24:19.340 --> 00:24:21.620
Next time: Commence Special Training!

00:24:22.060 --> 00:24:24.100
Run to the stage of your dreams!
